// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Logo 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P921010590" "Page from a strange diary"
// DetailString :
"P1565499740" "This torn page reads: <br><br>'I hear them chattering constantly in my mind: the minions of Igneous. Am I going crazy? I am beginning to understand their strange language. I believe the word 'logo' means 'home.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PoliceStory 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3157788591" "Officer Jaffney's story"
// DetailString :
"P1994270005" "One of the policemen you rescued told you: <br><br>'One of the Trolls said something about carrying us away to the slave camp. We've always known that the Trolls are forcing human prisoners to mine for them deep within the Hollows. But we've never known the extent of that practice. {HeroName}, I think the Trolls may have many more human prisoners than we ever guessed!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - Hollows_Flux_StoryArc_Souvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P935150707" "Flux the Outcast"
// tDetailString :
"P2392038770" "You met him out in the Hollows, not the nicest of guys, could use a shave and a shower, but there was something about Flux that told you he was on the right side. He was a spy, infiltrating the Outcasts in the hope of bringing them down. It's rare that you see that kind of dedication towards a single enemy. At least in that you can respect him.<br><br>At first, the missions Flux gave you were nothing more than errands any beginning hero could perform. But then, Flux let you into his confidence.<br><br>Frostfire, founder of the Outcasts was set in your sights. To think this guy once considered himself a hero. How far we fall sometimes. You defeated him. It wasn't your easiest fight, but you managed it. As you looked down at his body, you get the briefest flash of yourself in his position. 'It could happen to any of us', a voice inside your head tells you. Before you leave Frostfire, you rip off that stupid little emblem on his T-Shirt as a reminder of what could happen.<br><br>'Not to me, you think' as you walk away, hopefully never looking back."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3517719557" "Check it, I've got a hot tip today. Some of my 'buddies' in the Outcasts are planning a raid on a warren infested with Trolls. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>If you can get there, you can put a lot of bad guys in jail.</a> If you can't? Well, the caverns around the Hollows are anything but stable, and the Outcasts are hoping to bring that cave crashing down on the Trolls. Just in case their powers aren't enough, they've brought along a couple of bombs to finish the job."
// AcceptString :
"P3113042904" "Stop the Outcasts' raid on the Troll cave"
// SendOffString :
"P3640694591" "This could get ugly, {HeroName}. The Trolls may be on the wrong side of the law, but I don't want to see them buried alive."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3360387530" "Defeat gang leaders & crews"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1723397159" "If those caverns collapse, it'll be on your head and mine. Don't let that happen."
// TaskTitle :
"P3518425207" "<color deepskyblue>Flux the  Outcast</color>"

